@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity
@using System.Security.Claims
@inject eInvWorld.Data.ApplicationDbContext DbContext
@*
    Supplier role navigation (Tabler). Mirrors the Admin navigation's collapsible dropdown-group
    pattern and module naming exactly (Invoice Management, Item Management, Buyers Management,
    Company Management) so the sidebar UX and labels are consistent across roles. Unique ids per
    submenu (no duplicate DOM ids). Resolves the caller's own company id (same query as before) for
    the "My Company" link. Cosmetic only — authorization is enforced server-side and unchanged.

    Grouped into OVERVIEW / E-INVOICING / MASTER DATA / COMPANY section headers (Phase 1E nav
    reorganization). REPORTS and HELP sections from the redesign plan are intentionally omitted:
    no report or help/support page exists for the Supplier role today, so there is nothing to link
    to — add the section headers back when those pages ship.

    "+ Create" deep-links: Credit/Debit/Refund Note always require an existing source invoice
    (LHDN requires a referencing document for these types — see CreateInvoice.cshtml.cs's
    isAdjustmentDocCreation, which needs both a type AND a uuid), so unlike Invoice/Self-Billed
    Invoice there is no valid "blank" CN/DN/RN to deep-link to. That item routes to the Invoice
    List instead, where "Issue CN/DN" already exists as a per-invoice row action.
*@
@{
    string? companyId = null;
    var userId = User.FindFirstValue(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier);
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(userId))
    {
        companyId = DbContext.UserCompanies
            .Where(uc => uc.UserId == userId)
            .Select(uc => uc.PartyInfoId.ToString())
            .FirstOrDefault();
    }
}
